desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Broken Input Line"
	title_zh: "Broken Input Line"
	type: portability
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-portability-broken-input-line"
	risk: "code-style"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
'input_line' leaves a '\r' (CR) character when reading lines from a Windows text file, whose lines end in "\r\n" (CRLF). This is a problem for any Windows file that is being read either on a Unix-like platform or on Windows in binary mode. If the code already takes care of removing any trailing '\r' after reading the line, add a '(* noqa *)' comment to disable this warning.

### 风险类型
代码规范与兼容性（code-style）

### 影响
使用了已废弃、不兼容或不符合规范的模式，可能导致后续维护困难或运行环境差异。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
改用推荐 API 或兼容写法，并按照项目规范统一代码风格。
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.ml": <<<POS
input_line
POS
	"safefile://pos.ml": <<<NEG
In_channel.input_all
NEG
)

${*.ml}.pattern_regex(/(?:input_line)/) as $p0
${*.mli}.pattern_regex(/(?:input_line)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Broken Input Line",
	title_zh: "Broken Input Line",
	message: "Broken Input Line detected.",
}
